#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Leverage trim SQD for improved configuration selection for the latest "
"version of Sample-based quantum diagonalization (SQD)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Leverage trim SQD for improved configuration selection"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<OpenInLabBanner notebookPath=\"addons/qiskit-addon-sqd/guides/trim-"
"sqd.ipynb\" />\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The default behavior of "
"[`diagonalize_fermionic_hamiltonian`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-"
"addon-sqd/fermion) is to diagonalize each subsampled batch and keep the best"
" result. **Trim SQD** instead treats the batches as candidates to be "
"screened: each is diagonalized, *trimmed* down to the configurations "
"carrying the largest weight, and the survivors of all the batches are merged"
" and diagonalized together. That merged diagonalization is the one whose "
"energy the iteration reports, and its own trimmed output seeds the next "
"iteration.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The trim SQD implementation is based on joint research from\n"
"the Cleveland Clinic Foundation, RIKEN, and IBM&reg;. If you use this feature in\n"
"your research, also cite the paper. You can find the citation in the\n"
"`CITATION.bib` file, with citation key `merz2026crossing`.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For more details on the SQD code used in this example, see the [chemistry "
"Hamiltonian tutorial](/tutorials/sample-based-quantum-diagonalization).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Set up the molecule {#set-up-the-molecule}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Run the loop {#run-the-loop}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "One trim SQD iteration does the following:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Screening round.** Partition the bitstrings into batches.  Diagonalize "
"each batch and keep the `trim_ratio` fraction of its CI strings, per spin "
"sector, ranked by weight.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Merged round.** Diagonalize the merged survivors once. This is the result "
"the iteration reports, and its own trimmed strings seed the next "
"iteration.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The loop's `sci_solver` performs both rounds, and defaults to this package's"
" PySCF solver.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Enable trim SQD by passing the `TrimPolicy` as follows:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Check whether screening is helping {#check-whether-screening-is-helping}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Screening has the most to offer when the sampled configurations greatly "
"outnumber what can be diagonalized at once, so that ranking a larger pool "
"genuinely finds configurations a single batch would have missed. It has the "
"least to offer when a subspace of the affordable size already captures most "
"of the wavefunction.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Screening depends on the batches differing from one another. `TrimPolicy` "
"manages this by modifying the behavior of "
"`diagonalize_fermionic_hamiltonian` to draw one pool of `samples_per_batch *"
" num_batches` bitstrings and partitioning it among the batches, so no "
"bitstring appears in more than one.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Bound the subspace {#bound-the-subspace}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A subspace here is spanned by the *Cartesian product* of a spin-alpha and a "
"spin-beta CI string array.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Trimming ranks configurations, but the carryover is two per-spin string "
"lists. Keeping the 150 highest-weight configurations of a subspace typically"
" involves close to 150 distinct alpha strings and 150 distinct beta strings,"
" whose product spans roughly 22,500 configurations, not 150. So the subspace"
" handed to the next iteration is generally much larger than the set that was"
" ranked, and it grows quadratically in what you retain.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Trimming and carrying over are bounded separately, because they happen at "
"different points: trimming shrinks each batch of the screening round, while "
"the carryover is what crosses into the next iteration.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Four arguments bound it, and it is useful to set at least one:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**`trim_ratio`** is the fraction of each batch's strings, per spin sector, "
"that survive screening. Lower values shrink the merged subspace but discard "
"configurations the next iteration must rediscover by sampling.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**`max_strings_per_trim`** caps the strings each batch contributes, per "
"sector, regardless of the ratio. Useful with `symmetrize_spin`, which merges"
" both spin sectors into one list and so roughly doubles what each batch "
"offers. This bound is **per batch**: the merged subspace can hold up to "
"`num_batches` times as many strings, less whatever the batches had in "
"common, which in practice is not much.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**`carryover_threshold`**, **`carryover_ratio`**, and **`max_carryover`** "
"bound the strings that seed the next iteration, applied to the merged "
"subspace as a whole rather than per batch. `carryover_threshold` is the "
"amplitude cutoff that `StandardPolicy` uses, with the same default; the "
"other two bound the count, which the cutoff alone does not.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**`max_dim`**, on `diagonalize_fermionic_hamiltonian` itself, bounds each "
"spin sector of every subspace the loop diagonalizes, including the merged "
"one. It acts as a backstop and applies to whatever the policy returns, after"
" the carryover is merged with fresh samples.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The run above sets `max_strings_per_trim=250` and `max_dim=250` together, so"
" neither what each batch contributes nor the subspace built from it can run "
"away.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Use an external eigensolver {#use-an-external-eigensolver}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You can use trim SQD with an external eigensolver by passing the "
"`sci_solver` argument:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The prior snippet requires the `sbd-eigensolver` package to be installed "
"from PyPI.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Distribute the work {#distribute-the-work}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"With `TrimPolicy`, the loop calls `sci_solver` twice per iteration: once "
"with all the batches, and once with the merged subspace. Both calls go "
"through the ordinary `sci_solver` interface, which [this package's multi-"
"process support](/addons/qiskit-addon-sqd/guides/hpc-acceleration) invokes "
"collectively on every MPI rank.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Two levels of parallelism are potentially available, and they are "
"independent:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Within a diagonalization.** A solver such as SBD can spread a single "
"diagonalization across ranks.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Across the batches.** A solver could, in principle, diagonalize the "
"batches concurrently.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Given a set of batches, the solver determines how to delegate work to its "
"worker processes.\n"
msgstr ""
